menu "Keepsake Wi-Fi on demand"

    config KEEPSAKE_WIFI_ON_DEMAND
        bool "Keep the Wi-Fi radio off until network work needs it (experimental)"
        default n
        help
            Off (default): Wi-Fi behaves as it always has -- it connects at boot and stays
            connected -- and network jobs run whenever it is connected.

            On: the radio is off by default. Network jobs (time sync, transcription retries,
            and later weather, downloads and update checks) bring it up, run together, keep it
            on for 30 s in case more follow, then turn it off. With no known network in range
            it waits 30, then 60 minutes before trying again, but anything a person is waiting
            on tries straight away. The radio stays on while the Wi-Fi settings page or the
            setup hotspot is in use. See net_jobs::Scheduler (#17). Needs an on-device check
            before it becomes the default.

    config KEEPSAKE_NET_SYNC_INTERVAL_HOURS
        int "Background sync interval (hours)"
        depends on KEEPSAKE_WIFI_ON_DEMAND
        range 1 48
        default 6
        help
            How often, with Wi-Fi on demand, the radio comes up on its own to sync the time
            and send any recordings still waiting for transcription.

endmenu
